NimbyDevHarness (display name DevHarness) - original work by Jeff Fabish for
NIMBY | HARDCORE | BADLANDS | 1pp. No third-party mod code.

What it is: the dev harness of shared rules section 8. It is built only by
Build-NimbyPack.ps1 -Dev into build\@NIMBY-Dev-<stamp>\, signed with the separate
nimby_dev key, never listed in pack.json "addons", never part of the Workshop item,
and never loaded on the live server. It depends on NimbyAutorun and NimbyHands and
forges requests against their real server handlers; no client PBO references any
class defined here.

How it runs (server only):
- Boot cases run at mission start when $profile:NimbyDevHarness\selftest exists
  (the boot check creates it). They need no client: two survivor dummies and a few
  items are spawned, used, and deleted. Each case prints
  "[NIMBY][DevHarness][SelfTest] PASS|FAIL <case> detail=<text>" and the run ends
  with "[NIMBY][DevHarness] selftest complete; cases=N failures=M".
- Online cases need a connected player (a real identity). They run ten seconds
  after a player connects when $profile:NimbyDevHarness\forge contains the word
  "online", print "[NIMBY][DevHarness][Forge] PASS|FAIL <case> detail=<text>", and
  end with "[NIMBY][DevHarness] forge complete; cases=N failures=M". The two Hands
  stale-request cases use the item in the connecting player's hands (hold one) and
  pass the party checks only with a second connected player as the receiver.
- The dummies carry no identity, so a dummy giver or receiver fails the party
  check ("disconnected") before any later fact; the dummy cases therefore prove
  the ownership, consent, in-flight, step-2 guard, and switch branches, not the
  receiver-space branch, which the in-game V3 diagnostic and the forced-refusal
  run cover.
- The forge file word "step2-refuse" arms one forced Hands step-2 refusal at mission
  start (cost path B): the next real transfer ends
  "REFUSED detail=no space in receiver inventory (forced by dev harness); item with
  giver at ...".

